  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6d5e4d6f-a806-4049-9173-775493f7a7b9-image.png\" style=\"width: 141px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Assume a complete sphere, then&nbsp;flux&nbsp;due to a charge placed at the center of sphere is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Flux through hemisphere surface is equal to flux passing through flat surface&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d7d5ab33-b1aa-435f-a269-bf2b9d99640d-image.png\" style=\"width: 147px; height: 110px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
